{"title":"Squeeze Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Squeeze Theorem</b> (also called the <b>Sandwich Theorem</b> or the <b>Squeeze Play Theorem</b>) is a relatively simple <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Theorem\" title=\"Theorem\">theorem</a> that deals with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">calculus</a>, specifically <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Limit\" title=\"Limit\">limits</a>.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Squeeze_theorem_example.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/Squeeze_theorem_example.jpg/300px-Squeeze_theorem_example.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"292\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/20/Squeeze_theorem_example.jpg 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption>Squeeze Theorem</figcaption></figure>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Applications_and_examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Applications and examples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Squeeze_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Neighborhood\" title=\"Neighborhood\">neighborhood</a> of the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> approach some common limit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589b199482651099f9a270bc0511744fe918dde6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to S}f(x)=L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Squeeze_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in the neighborhood of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, then either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5c49b0c3b10a92842e56fee02006522ad2625c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)\\leq f(x) \\leq h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ebccf83feaaaf8744b73f659ce6cc9fff5dc1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)\\leq f(x)\\leq g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in this neighborhood.  The two cases are the same up to renaming our <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">functions</a>, so assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5c49b0c3b10a92842e56fee02006522ad2625c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)\\leq f(x) \\leq h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We must show that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4aedf4f18c620d464565f8a52547a478421a97dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4b1ee77622f50ac112610b5be1c8feb031ef31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c76108491d911a7d19a4c7aa9935d58e51625ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-S|&lt;\\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f58550b4f8668d1b407c77ba13dfd98d118150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(x)-L|&lt;\\varepsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793592cec6d3780cd294c4fb42d69c5917608a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to S}g(x)=\\lim_{x\\to S}h(x)=L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"25\" />, there must exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e0dcbf62b10151131b7478723da84e44afafdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta_1,\\delta_2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0b9eee7b3368e1fef612e618fbe1fc05954332.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x-S|&lt;\\delta_1 \\Rightarrow |g(x)-L|&lt;\\varepsilon \\textrm{  and  } |x-S|&lt;\\delta_2 \\Rightarrow |h(x)-L|&lt;\\varepsilon.\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a01948a42e4a9e0f723c6c9f80c77779c02f0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta = \\min\\{\\delta_1,\\delta_2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c76108491d911a7d19a4c7aa9935d58e51625ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-S|&lt;\\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc55cbfda775162d56980aef8001152d8799333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\varepsilon &lt; g(x) - L \\leq f(x) - L \\leq h(x) - L &lt; \\varepsilon.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f58550b4f8668d1b407c77ba13dfd98d118150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(x)-L|&lt;\\varepsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. Now by the definition of a limit we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589b199482651099f9a270bc0511744fe918dde6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to S}f(x)=L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Applications_and_examples\">Applications and examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Squeeze_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Applications and examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Squeeze Theorem can be used to evaluate limits that might not normally be defined. An example is the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5c8e97896b09f5f1c31d838edb84bce1d444e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^2 e^{\\sin\\frac{1}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" />  with the limit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f6759b997fe99031c55137363f92a98e7fd580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to 0} f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"24\" />. The limit is not normally defined, because the function oscillates infinitely many times around 0, but it can be evaluated with the Squeeze Theorem as following. Create two functions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466763d8093c6aab3836e9df67ceffcc6a2d4936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^2$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. It is easy to see that around 0, the function in question is squeezed between these two functions, and the limit as both of these approach 0 is 0, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f6759b997fe99031c55137363f92a98e7fd580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to 0} f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"24\" /> is 0.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Squeeze_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Squeeze_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Limit\" title=\"Limit\">Limit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">Calculus</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234932\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 211/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6836/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.619      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.619      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5739:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234932 and revision id 73416. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}